  "body": "Currently, a document is kept render-blocked until parser inserts a `body` element, even if there's no render-blocking element. This is controlled by the [awaiting parser-inserted body flag](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#awaiting-parser-inserted-body-flag).\r\n\r\nThis seems too stringent. There are some websites (e.g., facebook.com) that set `document.body` before parser inserts body. Their first paint will be delayed unnecessarily (and possibly by a large amount) if they are render-blocked until parser inserts body. See crbug.com/1303210 for more details.\r\n\r\nSo I think we should relax this. In particular, we can start rendering as long as the document's body element is non-null and all render-blocking resources have been loaded.\r\n\r\nI'll put up a PR for this.\r\n",
